.TH XIL\-SFX\-HYDRATE "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-sfx\-hydrate \- write pipe\-hint source paths from a parsed JSON into the matching SFX config
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-sfx\-hydrate
[\-h] (\-\-episode TAG | \-\-tag TAG) [\-\-show SHOW] [\-\-parsed FILE]
[\-\-sfx FILE] [\-\-dry\-run]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the
.B sfx_source
fields embedded in a parsed JSON and copies those source paths into the
matching
.B sfx_<TAG>.json
effects configuration.  This is useful after re\-parsing a script that
contains pipe\-hint annotations (e.g.
.BR "[SFX: STATIC | sfx_static.mp3]" )
when you want the SFX config to reflect the hints without regenerating the
full config from scratch.
.PP
Existing effects that already have a
.B source
field are left unchanged unless the parsed JSON carries a different hint.
With
.B \-\-dry\-run
the changes are reported but not written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-episode\fR \fI\,TAG\/\fR
Episode tag (e.g. S04E04).  Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-tag\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fI\,TAG\/\fR
Raw non\-episodic content tag (e.g. V01C03).  Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-episode\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI\,SHOW\/\fR
Show name override (default: from project.json)
.TP
\fB\-\-parsed\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Override the parsed JSON path (default: derived from episode/tag)
.TP
\fB\-\-sfx\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Override the SFX config path (default: derived from episode/tag)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report source fields that would be written without modifying the SFX config
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Hydrate the SFX config from a freshly parsed script:
.B xil sfx\-hydrate \-\-episode S01E02
.TP
Preview changes without writing:
.B xil sfx\-hydrate \-\-episode S01E02 \-\-dry\-run
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-parse (1),
.BR xil\-sfx (1),
.BR xil\-produce (1)
